[
  {
    "id": "ccf80ff9d2f512ab",
    "text": "1. Navigate to the \"Machine\" menu and click \"Machine Configuration Management\".",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "d996cf9aab883540",
    "text": "2. Click the \"Add a custom machine\" button.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "02aaa5f9ef8586ef",
    "text": "3. Fill in the information as shown below.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "1da4adaa2fd34301",
    "text": "4. Select the post processors just imported and set the \"Carvera ATC (mm)(*.cnc)\" as default.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "59fc09e14027c440",
    "text": "5. Click \"Apply\" then \"OK\" to save the configuration.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "61ce094a2de2cceb",
    "text": "Install Tool Database",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "4c63cf1412044bb5",
    "text": "1. Navigate to the \"Toolpaths\" menu and click \"Tool Database\".",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "baf9ffbcca3f2c17",
    "text": "2. Click the \"Import a tool database\" button.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "60e04960c43c95a8",
    "text": "3. Select the \"CarveraTools.vtdb\" file.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "5c4f851d9df65ce6",
    "text": "4. Click the \"Merge\" button on the popup confirm dialog and finish the import.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "b691ac5f508c63d9",
    "text": "Using VCarve Desktop Profiles",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "8521d352a8e09919",
    "text": "When saving Tool paths, select Carvera Desktop CNC Machine and a suitable post processor for your job.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/software/vcarve-desktop"
  },
  {
    "id": "dbcb3161f6870b5c",
    "text": "Milling Spindle - 3.175mm (1/8\") Shank Diameter Bits",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/speeds-and-feeds"
  },
  {
    "id": "932b6ea696f530e7",
    "text": "The following recommended parameters are based on current tests. The machining speed with small diameter tools/hard materials should be slow and fast in opposite. We will conduct more tests and provide more detailed parameter recommendations in the future on our website.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/speeds-and-feeds"
  },
  {
    "id": "e4deac588d1c11d2",
    "text": "Please start the test from the lower limit of the parameter, and adjust them based on the test results. For additional information and support, check out our",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/speeds-and-feeds"
  },
  {
    "id": "b8ae3038aab2abe4",
    "text": "tutorials and guides.",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/speeds-and-feeds"
  },
  {
    "id": "fd4279c6045da4f3",
    "text": "*RPM: SpindleSpeed(RPM) / Feed: FeedRate(mm/min) / PFeed: PlungeFeedRate(mm/min) / DOC: Depth of Cut(mm)",
    "page": "https://wiki.makera.com/en/speeds-and-feeds"
  },
